     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Is it possible or even sensible to use qplot for multiple time-series?<div><br></div><div>I have 3 series that I want to plot against time. Note that the series are over-lapping in time but some are longer than others.</div><div><br></div><div>If the answer is that it is best to do this using ggplot, that&#39;s fine too. I just thought I might be able to do it more quickly and simply in qplot.</div><div><br></div><div>Here is a short sample of my data, where it overlaps.</div><div><div>           UK.GDP     Index Penarth</div></div><div>135 -1.829215e+00  7.023564      NA</div><div><div>136 -2.000000e+00  7.396577      NA</div><div>137 -2.157312e+00  7.504081      NA</div><div>138 -2.272143e+00  7.118103    3.05</div><div>139 -2.300000e+00  8.191180    3.78</div><div>140 -2.203175e+00  7.646800    3.90</div><div>141 -1.971102e+00  8.680272    5.57</div><div>142 -1.600000e+00  9.723807    9.12</div><div>143 -1.107765e+00 10.301958   10.79</div><div>144 -5.990039e-01 11.311894   11.36</div><div>145 -2.000000e-01 12.332425   12.47</div><div>146  4.606072e-03 12.638204   12.80</div><div>147  9.674731e-02 13.434035   11.10</div><div>148  2.000000e-01 15.005981   10.82</div><div>149  3.967482e-01 13.506910    9.96</div><div>150  6.046072e-01 13.055482   10.03</div><div>151  7.000000e-01 11.213134    9.71</div><div>152  6.084010e-01 10.285893    9.10</div><div>153  4.514904e-01 11.134351   10.74</div><div>154  4.000000e-<a href=\"tel:+223%2020%2001%2010%2096\" value=\"+22320011096\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">01 12.232001   10.96</a></div><div>155  5.696478e-01 10.690246   10.42</div><div>156  8.560977e-01 10.239965   10.79</div><div>157  1.100000e+00 10.276742   10.69</div><div>158  1.168563e+00  7.975866    8.20</div><div>159  1.035230e+00  8.451590    8.72</div><div>160  7.000000e-01  8.395220    8.77</div><div>161  2.005433e-01  8.337025    8.09</div><div>162 -2.747948e-01  7.902604    6.47</div><div>163 -5.000000e-01  